        {
          "id": 3296267551,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "My kingdom for a language that has ways of creating variable-length expandable arrays, of values of arbitrary types, within the language. (Extra credit for allowing different styles of memory allocation, e.g. allocation from a specific pool that can be bulk-freed, at least until \"worrying about styles of memory allocation\" can be done by the compiler just as \"worrying about register allocation\" is now done by compilers.) That way, you don't lose the type-checking.\n\n(I think we *are* using such a language in the UI code, but expanding its use might be a bit of work.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-04-28T19:20:44.487Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-04-29T07:51:38.511Z",
