        {
          "id": 3296332373,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> It looks like we only use wmem_array_try_index in the MQ dissector; I'm surprised we don't use that in more places.\n\nIt was used until recently in the various LZ77 decompression routines (for which it was introduced), but removed as part of a recent optimization of those.\n\nIt not being part of the original wmem_array API is possibly a reason why it's not used so much.",
          "author": {
